e/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/database-repair/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "571ee7e4f8997fdfae74f800edd84d0efce760607b5043aa85a8d9d81962095f" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/database-repair/verification.json" "basis" 653} {"question" "q-15664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/assets/e4b9bd92b63d85b0336974285b6aa7a8a7beb8348cf368f65d805f7b4b70ffa2.png)\n\nGiven the plots of $y=f(x)$ and $y=g(x)$ above, find ${h}^{′}(1)$ where $h(x)=\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cd68b9304d49b4b5231c420eeb515dd50f5f50ef350bfabebf2740c72340a6" "basis" 379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The quotient rule for derivatives gives\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(x)=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)\\cdot g(x)-f(x)\\cdot {g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(1)=\\frac{{f}^{′}(1)\\cdot g(1)-f(1)\\cdot {g}^{′}(1)}{(g(1))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFrom the graph above, we obtain that $f(1)=3$ and $g(1)=2.$\n\nAdditionally:\n\n- The slope of $f(x)$ on $x\\in (0,2)$ equals $1.$ So, ${f}^{′}(1)=1.$\n\n- The slope of $g(x)$ on $x\\in (0,3)$ equals $-1.$ So, ${g}^{′}(1)=-1.$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(1)\\cdot g(1)-f(1)\\cdot {g}^{′}(1)}{(g(1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 2-3\\cdot (-1)}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cd68b9304d49b4b5231c420eeb515dd50f5f50ef350bfabebf2740c72340a6" "basis" 379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "208712200c4fe521a74d6a493ffa4f56a575834babe060db489a57c0f12e7421" "basis" 379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15664" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cd68b9304d49b4b5231c420eeb515dd50f5f50ef350bfabebf2740c72340a6" "basis" 379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15664" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{5}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cd68b9304d49b4b5231c420eeb515dd50f5f50ef350bfabebf2740c72340a6" "basis" 379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15664" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{7}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cd68b9304d49b4b5231c420eeb515dd50f5f50ef350bfabebf2740c72340a6" "basis" 379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15664" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cd68b9304d49b4b5231c420eeb515dd50f5f50ef350bfabebf2740c72340a6" "basis" 379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15664" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cd68b9304d49b4b5231c420eeb515dd50f5f50ef350bfabebf2740c72340a6" "basis" 379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15664" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cd68b9304d49b4b5231c420eeb515dd50f5f50ef350bfabebf2740c72340a6" "basis" 379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-41944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\sqrt{2} & -3.2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d202b35250385a2fb2656559dcf5f4a0b5ce8cd4ea309239a368884332ab69c" "basis" 840 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-41944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $A$ is the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $B$ by the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}$ on the *left*, the result must be the $2$nd *row* of $B.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2\\sqrt{2} & -3.2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\sqrt{2} & -3.2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2\\sqrt{2} & -3.2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d202b35250385a2fb2656559dcf5f4a0b5ce8cd4ea309239a368884332ab69c" "basis" 840 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-41944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4365440057493f60dc29fe8f63f7736b97744b7a6b03774345cdab7e0f4a7dd7" "basis" 840 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-41944" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "5d202b35250385a2fb2656559dcf5f4a0b5ce8cd4ea309239a368884332ab69c" "basis" 840 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "